  "goodToKnow": "Der Optimismus is optimism: vorsichtiger Optimismus (cautious optimism), Zweckoptimismus (putting on a brave face). Germans are often stereotyped as pessimistic worriers (die German Angst), though surveys show most are personally optimistic while worrying about the country. Der Optimist is an optimist, and optimistisch means optimistic. The opposite is der Pessimismus. It has no plural."
